A||||2||BigBoyToys||Need Help locating where vacuum line goes?||||5||
Z||000000||BigBoyToys||07-10-2000||08:01 PM||||86 GT with stock 2.8 v-6 setup.<BR>Noticed a vacuum (soft rubber hose) line just hanging.<BR>Just below the coolant fill cap in the engine compartment is an electro-vacuum switch device with a cylindrical chamber facing the front of the car and a single vacuum line (the one in question)is attached to a nipple on the end of the cylinder, but the other end is what I found unattached. My question is where does this attach?<BR>In the emissions diagram on the inside rear deck lid I can identify the vacuum hose but it also has no indication to where it attaches. On the diagram the vaccum line is<BR>pictures on the far left with two lines going into a rectangle and one line exiting, but just hanging there. <BR>From what I can tell this is part of the EGR subsystem. The reason being that the thin hard vacuum line coming off the top of the EGR Valve snakes its way over to this electro-vacuum switch device and enters it from the rear of this unit.<BR>Any help with where the other end of this rubber vacuum hose should be attached would be very much appreciated. I am sure this description is as clear as mud, as I have spent much time searching the many post on the EGR topic with no luck. <BR>TIA,<BR>BBTs||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||07-10-2000||10:17 PM||||That hose eventually goes to the air filter canister. Check the lower right side just under the air filter canister..you should see a hose about 4 or 5 inches long that is twisted and then clamped onto a hardline...follow that hardline to about the upper middle part of the firewall...thats where the other end of that hose should go (provided we're talking about the same hose..I believe so by your description)...hope that helps.||||reg||2
Z||000002||BigBoyToys||07-11-2000||12:35 AM||||Thanks MY7Fieros that sounds like the one I am looking for! U DA MAN!!!||||reg||14
